{
  "name": "177. Fallbacks across drop-in routes, request types and governance refusals (fallback-coverage)",
  "description": "Request-level fallbacks beyond /v1 chat. Each row's primary fails for free on a model the provider does not have, or is refused by governance, and an openai/gpt-4o-mini fallback serves. The x-bifrost-routing-info-provider, x-bifrost-routing-info-is-fallback and x-bifrost-fallback-index headers must name the fallback.\n\nRows: (1) an unconfigured fallback (fireworks) is skipped and the next one serves as fallback 2, the skipped slot keeping its place; (2) /anthropic fails over and answers in the Messages shape; (3) the same while streaming; (4) /bedrock Converse fails over; (5) a primary the virtual key does not allow is refused by governance and still falls back, with none of the primary provider's headers on the answer; (6) embeddings fail over; (7) a streaming /v1/responses request fails over. Run with FEATURE=\"fallback-coverage\".",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "openai an unconfigured fallback is skipped and the next one serves, keeping its place in the chain - fallback-coverage",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "var h = function (name) { return pm.response.headers.get(name); };",
              "pm.test('the openai fallback served as fallback 2', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(h('x-bifrost-routing-info-provider'), pm.response.text().slice(0, 400)).to.eql('openai');",
              "  pm.expect(h('x-bifrost-routing-info-is-fallback'), pm.response.text().slice(0, 400)).to.eql('true');",
              "  pm.expect(h('x-bifrost-fallback-index'), pm.response.text().slice(0, 400)).to.eql('2');",
              "});"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/chat/completions",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "chat",
            "completions"
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"model\": \"openai/bifrost-harness-missing-model\",\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": \"Reply with the single word: ok\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"max_tokens\": 3,\n  \"fallbacks\": [\n    \"fireworks/accounts/fireworks/models/llama-v3p1-8b-instruct\",\n    \"openai/gpt-4o-mini\"\n  ]\n}"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "openai the /anthropic route fails over from a missing Claude model to an openai fallback - fallback-coverage",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "var h = function (name) { return pm.response.headers.get(name); };",
              "pm.test('the openai fallback served', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(h('x-bifrost-routing-info-provider'), pm.response.text().slice(0, 400)).to.eql('openai');",
              "  pm.expect(h('x-bifrost-routing-info-is-fallback'), pm.response.text().slice(0, 400)).to.eql('true');",
              "});",
              "pm.test('the fallback answer comes back in the Anthropic Messages shape', function () {",
              "  var j = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.expect(j.type, pm.response.text()).to.eql('message');",
              "  pm.expect(j.content, pm.response.text()).to.be.an('array').that.is.not.empty;",
              "});"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript"
          }
        }
      ],
